cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the NEVPT2
  method papers listed under references.
type: software
title: "nevpt2-gpu-demo: SC- and PC-NEVPT2 on the GPU, end to end"
abstract: >-
  Strongly- and partially-contracted NEVPT2 on the GPU. From a CASCI/CASSCF
  wavefunction (a CI vector plus MO integrals) it builds the active-space
  3-RDM and the two integral-contracted 4-RDM intermediates on the device,
  assembles the eight perturber-class energies there, and checks them against
  committed PySCF (SC) and block2 (PC) reference data to 1e-7. One source tree
  builds for NVIDIA (CUDA) or AMD (ROCm/HIP).
authors:
  - family-names: Lostica
    given-names: Michael
license: MIT
keywords:
  - NEVPT2
  - multireference perturbation theory
  - quantum chemistry
  - GPU
  - CUDA
  - HIP
  - ROCm
